  "about": {
    "section_title": "About",
    "disclaimer": "This is an unofficial fan project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed, or supported by Egosoft. Egosoft assumes no technical support or liability (e.g., for corrupted save games). Use at your own risk. All names, trademarks, and content related to X4: Foundations are the property of Egosoft or their respective owners.",
    "steam_link_html": "<a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/392160/X4_Foundations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X4: Foundations on Steam</a>",
    "github_link_html": "View this project on GitHub: <a href=\"https://github.com/lwhite12/x4-procurement-tool\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://github.com/lwhite12/x4-procurement-tool</a>",
    "built_from_title": "Built From",
    "built_from_hint": "This site's ship/ware data is generated from these exact versions of the game and every installed DLC, alongside this tool's own version:",
    "future_plans_title": "Future Plans",
    "future_plans_hint": "A few bigger features on the roadmap, not built yet:",
    "user_accounts_title": "User Accounts & Saved States",
    "user_accounts_body": "Right now, sharing a fleet list, ship loadout, or price override preset means generating a one-off link (see the Share button above). The plan is to eventually add real user accounts, so you can save and recall your own fleet lists, ship loadouts, and price override presets directly -- without needing to keep track of links.",
    "language_support_title": "Language Support",
    "language_support_body": "Ship and ware names/descriptions are currently only pulled from the game's English-language files. Support for reading other languages X4 itself supports is planned.",
    "local_install_title": "Running this locally against your own game install",
    "local_install_hint": "The hosted website covers the base game and all DLCs. The eventual goal of this is to run against a local install with any combination of DLCs/mods you want to use. However, this is untested so who knows if it works. If you want to try it, here's how:",
    "local_install_step1_html": "Clone the repository (see the GitHub link above) and install Python dependencies: <code>pip install -r requirements.txt</code>.",
    "local_install_step2_html": "Obtain <strong>XRCatTool</strong> (an egosoft first-party X4 catalog-extraction tool -- not included in this repository) and place it at <code>XTools_1.11/XRCatTool.exe</code> under the repo root, or modify the repo code to point to your cli path. <span class=\"modal-hint\">[link to the current XRCatTool download to be added here]</span>",
    "local_install_step3_html": "Run <code>python src/extract_game_data.py</code> to pull ship/equipment/ware data out of your local X4 installation's <code>.cat</code>/<code>.dat</code> catalogs. By default this expects the game installed at <code>C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Steam\\steamapps\\common\\X4 Foundations</code> -- edit <code>GAME_ROOT</code> at the top of that script if yours lives somewhere else.",
    "local_install_step4_html": "Run <code>python src/generate_ships_table.py</code> to build <code>data/x4.db</code> from the extracted files.",
    "local_install_step5_html": "Run <code>python src/api.py</code> and open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8000/</code>."
  },
